course: dictionary
lesson: 1275
title: Context clues: the bustard
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sometimes a text uses a name you have never heard before. Do not panic. Read the words around it, because they are its context, and they often give clues. «A great bustard has three toes on each foot and no back toe, because it walks on open ground and never perches.» The sentence is about feet and walking, so a bustard must be an animal that walks on the ground.
explain: Next, check the clues for what kind of thing it is. «The great bustard is one of the heaviest birds that can fly» tells you a bustard is a bird, and that it is big and heavy. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Then put your idea back into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Clues can also show how a creature behaves. «In spring a male great bustard turns his feathers inside out to look like a white fluffy ball, puffs up his throat and fans his tail, and females watch many males before choosing.» The males are showing off, so this is a bird that makes a display to attract a mate.
fact: A bustard is a large, heavy bird with long legs.
fact: Bustards live on grasslands and open plains, and they prefer to run rather than fly.
fact: The great bustard is one of the heaviest flying birds in the world.
fact: «Bustard» is a noun: a bustard, two bustards.
fact: Big males of the great bustard weigh about 16 kilograms, and the great bustard is listed in Ukraine's Red Book.
fact: The great bustard was wiped out in Britain, and it is being brought back on Salisbury Plain.
exercise: «A great bustard has three toes on each foot and no back toe, because it walks on open ground and never perches.» What is a bustard? | *A large, heavy bird with long legs that walks on grasslands | A tiny insect that hops between flowers | A tree that grows on mountains | A small fish that swims in rivers
exercise: «Big males weigh about 16 kilograms.» What does the word about show? | The bird weighs nothing at all | *The weight is an estimate, not exact | The bird is a female | The bird weighs exactly 16 kilograms
exercise: A bustard can fly, but it prefers to run. What does prefers mean? | Forced to | Afraid of | *Likes better | Forgets how to
test: «In spring a male great bustard turns his feathers inside out to look like a white fluffy ball.» What is the male doing? | Sleeping all day in the sun | Hiding in a river | *Showing off to attract a mate | Laying eggs in a tall tree
test: Where is the great bustard listed as a threatened species? | *In Ukraine's Red Book | In a book of Australian beaches | In a Scottish cookbook | In a dictionary of castles
exam: Which sentence best helps you work out what a bustard is? | *A great bustard has three toes on each foot and walks on open ground | The bird was brought back on Salisbury Plain | Females watch many males before choosing | The great bustard is one of the heaviest birds that can fly
